<title>USA: No damaging cold this week for Brazil coffee - WSC.</title>
<headline>No damaging cold this week for Brazil coffee - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>No damaging cold is expected this week in Brazil's coffee-growing areas, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Monday.</p>
<p>Monday and Tuesday would be dry, with temperatures near to above normal.</p>
<p>WSC said the outlook was for a chance of a few light showers on Wednesday, and generally dry conditions on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>Temperatures would be near to above normal.</p>
<p>East-central Brazil was dry on Sunday with highs of 68-88 F and conditions remained generally favourable for the trees and the maturing crop, WSC said.</p>
</text>
